ree, consistent with a Lean R race. Abbott's overwhelming financial edge and incumbency in a Republican-leaning state justify keeping the Republican ahead despite the tightening trend.", "watch": "A late shift in the national midterm environment or another round of polls showing Hinojosa within a point would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Greg Abbott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Greg Abbott seeks another term against state Representative Gina Hinojosa in a race that has tightened considerably in the final weeks. Polls from late October consistently show Abbott ahead, but by modest margins of roughly two to five points, with several surveys putting the gap near three points. Ratings from nonpartisan analysts cluster at Lean Republican, with one calling it a Tossup.\n\nThe financial picture strongly favors the incumbent: Abbott has raised over $25 million and holds $67 million on hand, boosted by a $5 million donation from Elon Musk, while Hinojosa has raised about $6 million. Prediction markets give Hinojosa roughly a one-in-three chance. The race remains competitive but leans Republican heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2717, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2616, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2248, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2304, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2288, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.255, "margin": -3.0}, {"dat